            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Foreign Relations</strong><br>\nMao's era saw fluctuating relationships with foreign powers, including a partnership and later a split with the Soviet Union and an eventual rapprochement with the United States in the 1970s.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Succession</strong><br>\nMao died on September 9, 1976. His death ended a revolutionary era. The subsequent leadership moved to reform China's economy and open it to the world.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Mao's Legacy</strong><br>\nMao Zedong is one of history's most transformative figures. His governance resulted in profound changes in China, with a legacy that is deeply complex, marked by both achievement and controversy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
